// This message file contains text to be used in game-supplied telegrams.
// Only the message line numbers 1000 or higher are valid
// Each new telegram begins on a multiple of 10, and can use up to 10
// lines, which must be consecutive. Each line appears in the telegram
// in one big paragraph, with the word STOP between each line
// The first two blocks, at 1000 and 1010, are reserved for UI use

{1000}{CLASS OF}
{1001}{SERVICE}
{1002}{Class A Good}
{1003}{Class B Fair}
{1004}{Class C Poor}
{1005}{Tarant Union}
{1006}{Telegraph}
{1007}{SYMBOLS}
{1008}{ST-Stop}
{1009}{ET-End}

{1010}{NR-No Response}
{1011}{NO RESPONSIBILITY is assumed by this Company, beyond the exercise of due diligence and good faith in the transmission of messages, but their best exertions of their own line, which is in the city of Tarant.}
{1012}{ STOP }

// Telegram to Player from Mayor of Grayhills asking for help
{1020}{Dear Brave Adventurer,
STOP Our small town of Grayhills is in need of an adventurer STOP A Mummy was sited on the outskirts of our town by a local farmer STOP We fear that the Mummy poses a serious threat to our safety STOP

We would appreciate it if you could sail to Grayhills with all due haste STOP I feel that the Mummy must be dealt with before it is too late STOP We will gladly compensate you for your trouble with an agreeable amount of coin STOP

Yours sincerely,
The Mayor of Grayhills}

// Telegram which the Mayor has. It details the cargo of 'The Crescent Wave'
{1030}{TARANT CUSTOMS OFFICE

ATTN: The Mayor of Grayhills,
STOP The ship 'The Crescent Wave' has set sail from Tarant STOP Expected time of arrival in Grayhills is 1 week STOP

Cargo as Inspected by Customs:

Food Supplies .......... 1 Week
Total Goods ......... 2672 Stone
Passengers ................... 1

STOP Direct any queries to the Tarant Customs Office, Tarant}